  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "A native of Key Biscayne, Florida, Devaney studied finance and English at Colorado State University. He began as a mortgage-securities analyst and trader, then founded United Capital Markets in 1999 to provide research and liquidity in complex asset-backed bonds. The firm expanded from a small island office into brokerage, asset-management and hedge-fund operations serving illiquid structured-credit markets.\n\nDevaney made and lost fortunes around the subprime mortgage cycle, rebuilding through distressed bonds and commercial real estate rather than leaving the field. United Capital Markets later traded residential and commercial mortgage securities, collateralised debt products and aircraft-backed paper. He broadened his work through Manor House Films, producing projects centred on addiction, redemption and child trafficking, while supporting mentoring and community-building initiatives in Florida and the Bahamas.",
    "html": "<p>A native of Key Biscayne, Florida, Devaney studied finance and English at Colorado State University. He began as a mortgage-securities analyst and trader, then founded United Capital Markets in 1999 to provide research and liquidity in complex asset-backed bonds. The firm expanded from a small island office into brokerage, asset-management and hedge-fund operations serving illiquid structured-credit markets.</p>\r\n<p>Devaney made and lost fortunes around the subprime mortgage cycle, rebuilding through distressed bonds and commercial real estate rather than leaving the field. United Capital Markets later traded residential and commercial mortgage securities, collateralised debt products and aircraft-backed paper. He broadened his work through Manor House Films, producing projects centred on addiction, redemption and child trafficking, while supporting mentoring and community-building initiatives in Florida and the Bahamas.</p>\r\n",
